WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.378
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.378 --> 00:00:12.230
One morning, six years ago, I woke up
with an overwhelming feeling of dread.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.979
I was beginning to feel more and more
suffocated by my life as an accountant.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.940
You see, I had chosen this life, but

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.320
I felt no sense of meaning,
no sense of purpose.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.040
Not only was I unfulfilled,
but I was falling apart.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:35.940
And as I showered that morning,
I thought to myself,

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.970
if I died today, it wouldn't be so bad.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.280
I went to work that morning.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.070
I sat at my desk and I work on my
spreadsheets like I did every other day.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:53.850
And at the end of the day, I packed up
my stuff and I drove to go back home.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.820
But on that specific day on
the drive back, everything changed.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.970
As I was going down the freeway
at 70 miles per hour,

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.990
a big white truck that was in front of me
swerved to avoid a broken down minivan.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.010
I didn't have time to get out of the way,
so

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:12.840
I crashed head first,
into the back of a car.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.050
As the windscreen shattered,
I closed my eyes and

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.770
braced myself as my car was flung
viciously into oncoming traffic.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.000
And in the chaos and noise,
the first thought that came to my head was

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.500
thank God,
I don't have to go to work tomorrow.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.730
As you can see I'm standing
in front of you today.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.630
I survived but in the days and weeks that
followed I thought to myself, what was

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.240
the point of surviving only to go back to
a life that made me feel like I was dying.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.210
And perhaps my case is extreme, but
maybe you felt something similar.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.023
A lack of fulfillment in your job, a lack
of fulfillment in your relationships.

00:01:54.023 --> 00:01:57.723
Just going through the motions,
surviving not quite thriving.

00:01:57.723 --> 00:02:02.323
Living not a full life, but a half one.

00:02:02.323 --> 00:02:05.641
And after my accident,
I realized yes we're given life,

00:02:05.641 --> 00:02:08.160
but we also have to choose it for
ourselves.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.800
You see we hear these stories of
work that doesn't feel like work.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.870
We hear these stories of epic and
beautiful love and if that was true,

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.412
I wanted that for myself as well.

00:02:16.412 --> 00:02:22.450
As Thoreau, the great poet once wrote,
I wished to live deliberately.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.980
I did not wish to live what was not life,
nor did I want to practice resignation.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.534
I wanted to live deeply and
suck all the marrow out of life.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:34.245
That is my intention.

00:02:37.653 --> 00:02:41.253
I didn't know how I was going to do it,
but I was determined to figure it out.

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:48.638
A couple weeks later, I stumbled upon
an interview with Oprah and Gary Zukav,

00:02:48.638 --> 00:02:52.510
author of the New York Times best
selling book, The Seat of the Soul.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.500
And the core message of the book struck
right to the center of my being.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.690
It said, in order to live an authentic and

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:02.240
fulfilling life, you have to align
your personality with your purpose.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.260
In order to live an authentic and

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.110
fulfilling life, you have to align your
personality with your soul's purpose.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:15.180
And according to the book, there
are three key step to make that happen.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.410
First, uncover your personality.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.750
So who are you deep down inside?

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.990
What are your values,
your motivations, what lights you up?

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.530
Two, use your personality
to find your purpose, and

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:30.460
turn that light from within outward
to be of service to other people.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:38.020
And third, take steps every single day to
live that personality and that purpose.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.240
So step one, uncover my personality.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.070
What would the person that I wanted to
become have to do to live a life that was

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:47.870
true to him?

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.210
After much thought,
I knew what my first act had to be.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:57.840
I would have to reveal to my
parents that I was what they,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.460
as Africans, would call evil.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:08.360
Unnatural, of the dark side, un-African.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:12.540
I would have to reveal to
my parents that I was gay.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.750
And I say this as if it was easy,
but it was incredibly difficult.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.140
But I was determined to not
hide any parts of my identity.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:29.090
And during this time, I decided to leave
my lucrative, but painful, accounting job.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:31.440
And despite strong
protests with my parents,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.360
I took three months off to travel
alone to seven Asian countries.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:39.770
I was seeking some kind of fulfillment,
some kind of awakening.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:40.630
And as a way to capture and

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.730
share those experiences,
I decided to film a video blog.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:48.730
And to my great surprise,
I discovered my deep, deep love for

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:52.650
using video as a way to capture and
share experiences with other people.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:56.460
&gt;From hunting down the most delicious
ramen in the backseats of Kyoto,

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.530
to trying to recreating my very
own Eat Pray Love moment in Bali.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.015
Which, by the way, is not a thing.

00:05:03.015 --> 00:05:07.440
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But I felt fulfilled, I felt alive.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.470
You see, video allowed me to show and
not have to tell.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.380
To be, and not have to perform.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.840
I could just be my most authentic form.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.510
Who would you be in your
most authentic form?

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:20.410
What would you be doing?

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:24.760
What purpose might you stumble upon?

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.771
You see, as I created these videos I
felt something I hadn't thought before,

00:05:28.771 --> 00:05:33.550
a deeper sense of connection to the young
Africans that were watching my videos.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.740
This was step two in action.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:41.160
My commitment to uncover my
personality led me right to my purpose

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.360
which is to inspire and entertain
young Africans through online video.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.630
There is nothing else in
the world that I'd rather do.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.750
What I know now in hind sight
is that it's the commitment.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:55.640
The commitment to wanting
a better relationship.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:58.730
The commitment to wanting
a more fulfilling job.

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:02.420
The commitment to finding your
purpose is the most important step.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.960
As Gerta,
the famous German writer once wrote,

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.720
until one is committed, there is
hesitancy, the chance to draw back.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:16.170
But the moment one definitely commits
oneself, then Providence moves, too.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:20.138
You see, when we commit we see things
we otherwise wouldn't have seen.

00:06:20.138 --> 00:06:24.198
We make connections we
otherwise wouldn't have made

00:06:24.198 --> 00:06:29.078
the moment one commits oneself,
then Providence moves, too.

00:06:37.918 --> 00:06:39.600
So what did I have to do next?

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:43.818
I had to figure out what
I was going to commit to.

00:06:43.818 --> 00:06:46.258
What are you willing to commit to today?

00:06:46.258 --> 00:06:48.538
Right here, right now.

00:06:51.038 --> 00:06:54.582
Before my accident, I was lost and
hopeless as an accountant, but

00:06:54.582 --> 00:06:58.824
after my travels, I felt alive, I felt
fulfilled, the feeling was cellular,

00:06:58.824 --> 00:07:00.430
I could feel it, it was real.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.070
When you commit to uncovering your
personality and your purpose,

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:07.330
I have no doubt that that is possible for
you, too.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.450
That brings me to step three.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.830
Discovery of your purpose is necessary,
but

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.140
not sufficient to live an authentic and
fulfilling life.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:22.140
You have to take the steps
to live it every single day.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:27.675
So because I like online video,
I set my sights on Hollywood.

00:07:27.675 --> 00:07:30.330
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; The lights, the camera, the action.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:34.090
But from my home in South Africa,
Hollywood seemed too far away.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.970
And I could have stopped, but I didn't.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.520
I had committed.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:42.500
And what I know now is that the most
successful people just start exactly

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.670
where they are.

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:47.640
So I started my very own YouTube
show with my best friend, Lindy.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:51.650
Dedicated to sharing stories with young
Africans just like myself, everything from

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:56.960
serious to funny topics, like interracial
dating, what it means to be African

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.684
in modern times, and even the trials and
tribulations of black girls' hair.

00:08:01.684 --> 00:08:04.610
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And I know it's easy to just say,

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:07.400
I'll just start my own YouTube show,
but it's incredibly hard.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:10.730
You see,
building an online following is tough, but

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:15.520
facing my inner doubts and
outter critics is even harder.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:19.760
&gt;&gt; To this day,
I still receive homophobic comments.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.700
Things like why would you share this
video with me this guy looks scared

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:27.790
I don't want to see stuff like that,
and what that has tought me is

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:31.340
that authenticity is not all upside
&gt;&gt; You will get beaten

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:33.080
down in the process.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.823
But instead of feeling like I was dying,
I was living.

00:08:36.823 --> 00:08:41.541
A show that I created in my
bedroom was watched by over 10,000

00:08:41.541 --> 00:08:43.658
people in 150 countries.

00:08:43.658 --> 00:08:46.340
The show has paved a brick
road of blessings for me.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:51.220
I have so many supporters
who have become super fans,

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:56.690
some who have even become friends,
and one of those friends is Laura.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:01.180
Laura is a super fan from Zimbabwe,
and because I like to get to know my

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.640
super fans,
I set up a time to Skype call with her.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.460
Little did I know the impact
this call would have on my life.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:10.330
It turns out that Laura
is a little person.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.390
And that because of the show,
she was inspired to start her very

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:17.650
own YouTube show and the Little People's
Association for Zimbabwe, a place for

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:20.900
little people to come together,
share stories, and inspire each other.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:27.588
She told me that because of my show,
she knew that she was enough.

00:09:27.588 --> 00:09:34.153
As Marianne Williamson, the author,
once wrote, as we let our own light shine,

00:09:34.153 --> 00:09:39.503
we unconsciously give other people
the permission to do the same.

00:09:39.503 --> 00:09:40.965
When we choose life,

00:09:40.965 --> 00:09:45.530
we unconsciously give other people
the permission to do the same.

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.649
I went from being
a miserable accountant and

00:09:49.649 --> 00:09:54.720
now an inspired YouTube produce with a
mission to light up other people's lives.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.090
I'm even building a company
with that mission.

00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.260
Who are you now?

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:01.020
Who could you be?

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.700
With a commitment to uncovering
your personality and your purpose,

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.480
imagine what you could do,
how big you could play.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.820
And in the time since my journey began,

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:17.220
I've learned that playing big in the world
doesn't have to mean being the CEO of

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:21.495
the next best startup in Silicon Valley,
or Beyonce at the Super Bowl.

00:10:21.495 --> 00:10:25.410
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Or starting your very own YouTube show.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.580
We can choose to play big every day
by having the courage to choose life,

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:33.160
by having the courage to uncover
our personality and our purpose.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:40.352
Because once you commit to choosing life,
I can assure you that Providence

00:10:40.352 --> 00:10:46.284
will move, too, and your light will give
other people the courage to do the same.

00:10:46.284 --> 00:10:47.084
Thank you.

00:10:47.084 --> 00:10:53.080
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.889
[MUSIC]

